# @@@AX25_SYSCONFDIR@@@/wampes.conf
#
# The WAMPES nodes this machine can reach.  One node per line:
#
#	name		address				description
#
# The name is what stands before the colon in an axports entry, so the
# entries wampes:hfb and wampes:70cm are two ports of the node "wampes".
# It is resolved here and never sent to the node.
#
# The address is either a path, for the node's unix socket, or host:port
# for its TCP service - which the node keeps switched off unless its
# net.rc says "start axtcp", because a TCP port carries no rights of its
# own.  Reach a node over TCP only where every local account may use the
# transmitter.
#
# The line for the node on this machine is the one that has to be right:
# its path is where the WAMPES on this machine put their socket, which is
# the TCPDIR they were built with, followed by /sockets/ax25.  This package
# was configured for @@@WAMPES_TCPDIR@@@, so the line below is right for a
# WAMPES that took the default; it is left commented out because a path that
# is only probably right is worse than one that has to be uncommented on
# purpose.  libax25 cannot know what a WAMPES was actually built with, so a
# WAMPES installed somewhere else wants its own line here.
#
# See wampes.conf(5) and axports(5).

#wampes		@@@WAMPES_TCPDIR@@@/sockets/ax25	the node on this machine
#db0aaa		192.168.1.5:8010		the club node, over TCP
#db0aaa-1	[fd00::5]:8010			db0aaa-1 over TCP IPv6
